\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Two columns and the reduced alternating form}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{In the matrix realization of \ref{fdip-00V7}, write
#{X=(x_1,x_2)} by columns. The map #{X\mapsto(x_1,x_2)}
is the explicit left-#{2T}-module isomorphism
##{\mathcal O/3\mathcal O\cong S\oplus S,\qquad
 S=\mathbb F_3^2.}
The Hurwitz fiber has rank #{4}; each column module has rank
two. Its full internal commutant is #{M_2(\mathbb F_3)^{\mathrm{op}}}
by \ref{fdip-00V5}, whereas the commutant on one column is
scalar by \ref{fdip-00V7}.}

\p{For the area form
#{\epsilon(u,v)=u_1v_2-u_2v_1}, reduction of the
[integral alternating Hurwitz form](fdip-00V2) is
##{b_{\mathbb F_3}(X,Y)=\epsilon(x_1,y_1)+\epsilon(x_1,y_2)
                         +\epsilon(x_2,y_1).}
Its multiplicity-space matrix is
#{\left(\begin{smallmatrix}1&1\\1&0\end{smallmatrix}\right)},
whose determinant is #{-1}. Thus this is a perfect alternating
form on the two-column module.}

\p{To calculate the specific form, let
##{C=Q_{\qi}+Q_{\qj}=\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\0&2\end{pmatrix}.}
The reduced trace #{t(z)=z+\bar z=2\operatorname{Re}(z)}
becomes ordinary matrix trace under \ref{fdip-00V7}, since
#{X+\adjugate X=(\trace X)\bbI}. Thus
##{b_{\mathbb F_3}(X,Y)=\tfrac{1}{2}\trace(\adjugate(X)YC).}
This reduction is legitimate over #{\mathbb Z[1/2]} and
then #{\mathbb F_3}, where #{1/2=2}. Expanding by columns,
##{\trace(\adjugate(X)YC)
 =-\epsilon(x_2,y_1)+2\epsilon(x_1,y_1)+2\epsilon(x_1,y_2).}
Multiplication by #{2} in #{\mathbb F_3} gives the displayed
three-term formula. Equivalently it reproduces the integer
Gram matrix modulo #{3} on the 4 basis images.}

\p{Setting #{X=Y} cancels the two mixed area terms and
kills the diagonal area term, proving alternation.
The tensor of the invertible area matrix with the displayed
invertible multiplicity matrix is invertible, proving
perfectness. Every unit image has determinant one by
\ref{fdip-00V7}, so it preserves #{\epsilon}; acting on both
columns proves invariance of the reduced form directly.}
